    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“Godhood is community service. I’m here to keep the lights on.”</em></p><p><strong>Manifesting (Delegated):</strong> You are a full prepared caster. Your manifesting is routed through stabilized civic thoughtforms (tulpas), retired gods, and the Long Quiet—reducing volatility and preventing raw backlash.</p><p><strong>Delegated Channeling:</strong> When you cast a manifestation, you treat esoteric misalignment as <em>neutral</em> (no penalty). When you cast in alignment with your Jurisdiction, you convert alignment into <strong>resources</strong> rather than raw power.</p><h3>Surge</h3><p>Your Surge bank is capped by tier (4 / 6 / 8 / 10). You bank <strong>+1 Surge per manifestation you sustain</strong> at the start of your turn (max +2), and spend it from the ◆ Surge menu — Invoke Clause, Binding Writ, Shelter the Bound, Sovereign Writ, and your doctrine's three spends. Everyone's Surge explodes the same way; yours arrives through contracts kept.</p><h3>Noise</h3><p>Pactkeepers do not suffer backlash; they accumulate <strong>Noise</strong> like every manifestant — acting outside your Jurisdiction, overriding consent, forcing outcomes. Noise follows the manifestation rules; several doctrine features add or remove it.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
